title The portfolio becomes a record
prompt Keaton gave two Squarespace payloads -- one day's receipts, then the full 126-item account list -- and asked to seat them, alongside a large naming round: nine synonyms for one Mycelium instantiation, the kres contract language season, and a GUI module named from a domain.
think Seated the portfolio first because it is the thing a naming round should read. Several names the tree already uses are in it, and a few names in it have no module yet, which is the useful half.
think Recorded the expired entry rather than dropping it. 199999999999.net reads EXPIRED 20260710 in the account listing, so the header states listed 126, expired 1, held 125. A registry that silently omits what lapsed teaches a reader the wrong thing about what the account contains.
think The serf/surf question resolved itself on Keaton's word: he holds both, surf-social.com is live, and the three serf spellings redirect to it. Surf stays the seated module name, so the Lexicon entry written this morning needed a note rather than a correction.
obs Stopped on the nine-synonym request and measured instead of executing. WAVE, WOV, MURR, MALA, and KYRI are all already seated, and KYRI is the voice and the notation -- it heads every session log in this tree. Declaring those nine synonyms of one Mycelium instantiation would make the tree's most central name mean three things.
obs That is the third naming request this session that would have recreated the exact ambiguity a prior rename removed. crux to construction split one word doing two jobs; cairn to checkpoint merged two senses deliberately and said so; this one would have merged five. The pattern is worth a rule: before a name is seated, grep it whole-word tree-wide and read the Lexicon, and if it is already seated say so before the word is spent.
obs MOX measures zero uses tree-wide -- the one genuinely free name of the nine, and the honest candidate for a Mycelium instantiation. TIDE, WOVN, and KYLI are nearly free at 9, 49, and 26.
loom registry listed=126 held=125 expired=1 roles_annotated=23 synonyms_checked=9 already_seated=5 free=1
file construction/domain-registry.bron the portfolio, with roles on the 23 that already mean something
file context/LEXICON.md the serf redirect recorded beside Surf Social
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- the registry is seated and green. The nine-synonym seating waits on your word because five of the nine are taken and one is Kyri; MOX is free and I would seat that alone. The kres contract language season, the macro-language work, and the GUI module name are design rounds rather than mechanical ones, and they belong in the expanded prompt that still wants writing.
